    "created": "2026-05-26",
    "updated": "2026-05-26",
    "body": "# Smol Gardens Project Presentors\n\nThe presentation and facilitation team for the [[Smol Gardens]] initiative at Makeshift 2026 Accountable Tech Conference (May 20, NYC x Design Week).\n\n## Team Roles\n\n### Krizia Fernando\n- **Role**: Project Author & Lead Presenter\n- **Contribution**: Core vision and framework for [[Smol Gardens]]\n- Introduces the initiative, articulates the accountability challenge in [[Civic Tech]]\n- Presents the impact framework (human, systems, environmental dimensions)\n\n### Priyanka Thomas\n- **Role**: Workshop Facilitator\n- **Contribution**: Leads hands-on workshop experience\n- Guides participants through applying the accountability framework\n- Facilitates \"diary mission\" where builders track their AI platform usage\n- Documents participant experiences\n\n### Kris Rubiano\n- **Role**: Tech Consultant & SmolLM Demo Lead\n- **Contribution**: Technical expertise in [[Small Language Models]]\n- Demonstrates practical use of SmolLM during workshop\n- Shows how to vibecode a simple AI application using SLMs\n- Guides evaluation process for impact assessment\n\n## Workshop Structure\n\nThe Makeshift NYC presentation includes:\n1. **Short presentation** on [[Smol Gardens]] project and accountability in [[Civic Tech]]\n2. **Framework introduction** — impact dimensions and design principles\n3. **Hands-on portion** — participants vibecode an AI app using SmolLM with guidance from Kris\n4. **Evaluation exercise** — assess impact across human, systems, and environmental dimensions with facilitation from Priyanka\n\n## Target Audience\n\nDesigners, builders, and civic technologists already using AI tools but feeling caught between pressure to move fast and need to build responsibly."
