    "body": "SubscribeSign in # The Humanities Are the Moat ### Twenty years of defunding the disciplines that teach judgement. Now we are surprised nobody can tell when AI is wrong. [ ![Dr Sam Illingworth's avatar](https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ocis!,w_36,h_36,c_fill,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9906c159-6ee4-41ae-b997-5d0c58d074a7_815x815.png) ](https://substack.com/@samillingworth) [Dr Sam Illingworth](https://substack.com/@samillingworth) Apr 08, 2026 196 9 64 Share The ability to evaluate what AI produces was never a technical skill. It was a humanities education. #### **In this post I will:** - Show how Melania Trump’s robot Plato accidentally exposed the case for the humanities in an AI world. - Argue that twenty years of defunding the…",
