    "body": "# Wiki Architecture\n\nThe three-layer structural design underlying the [[LLM Wiki Pattern]].\n\n## Layer 1: Raw Sources\n\nImmutable collection of curated source documents.\n\n- Articles, papers, PDFs, images, data files\n- User's source of truth\n- LLM reads but never modifies\n- Organized in `raw/` directory\n\n## Layer 2: The Wiki\n\nLLM-generated and maintained synthesis layer.\n\n- Markdown files organized by type: concepts, entities, syntheses, summaries\n- LLM owns this layer entirely\n- Creates pages, updates when new sources arrive\n- Maintains cross-references and consistency\n- User reads; LLM writes\n- Organized in `wiki/` directory with subdirectories:\n  - `wiki/concepts/` — concept pages\n  - `wiki/entities/` — people, organizations, projects\n  - `wiki/syntheses/` — analyses, comparisons, overviews\n  - `index.md` — catalog of all pages\n  - `log.md` — chronological record of ingests/queries\n\n## Layer 3: Schema Configuration\n\nA document (e.g., CLAUDE.md for Claude Code) that defines:\n\n- How the wiki is structured\n- Naming conventions and frontmatter format\n- Workflows for ingestion, querying, and maintenance\n- Rules and constraints for the LLM\n\nThis configuration makes the LLM a disciplined wiki maintainer rather than a generic chatbot.\n\n## Key Features\n\n**Index.md** — Content-oriented catalog, organized by category, enables search without embedding infrastructure at small scale (~100 sources, ~hundreds of pages)\n\n**Log.md** — Append-only chronological record of ingests, queries, and lint passes; parseable with unix tools\n\n## Related Concepts\n\n- [[LLM Wiki Pattern]] — the full pattern this architecture supports\n- [[Cross-referencing]] — how consistency is maintained across layers"
